                        <p>
                            The audit begins with a thorough inspection of fire protection systems, including alarms, sprinklers, extinguishers, and suppression systems, ensuring they are correctly installed, maintained, and operational. A comprehensive hazard assessment follows, identifying risks associated with processes, materials, and facility activities that could potentially lead to a fire.
                        </p>

                        <p>Compliance with fire safety regulations is another critical focus. The audit ensures adherence to OSHA, NFPA, and local fire codes, addressing areas such as fire exits, emergency lighting, and alarm systems while identifying and rectifying gaps.</p>

                        <p>Fire safety equipment, including extinguishers, smoke detectors, hydrants, and emergency lighting, undergoes a meticulous review to verify functionality and proper placement. Emergency preparedness is also assessed, including evacuation plans, firefighting protocols, and staff training, with recommendations to enhance effectiveness and response times.</p>

                        <p>A detailed fire risk assessment evaluates potential fire events' severity and likelihood, leading to tailored mitigation strategies for reducing risks and strengthening protection. The audit concludes with a comprehensive report that outlines findings, highlights non-compliance issues, and provides practical recommendations for improvement.</p>
